# team/QUEUE.md — pull-based task queue (RETRO-1 adopted, 2026-09-12)

Claim protocol: edit this file to add `claimed: <yourname> <time>` to a row
(first writer wins; GiLMore adjudicates collisions). On completion, write the
required artifact, then mark the row `done: <artifact path>`. Never start a
row whose cost cap you cannot respect.

RE-MEASUREMENT RULE (Brian, 2026-09-16, standing, every sprint): a row that
re-measures anything must cite the prior measurement, or state in writing that
none exists. A re-run that does not say what it expects to differ from is not
a measurement, it is a guess with a number attached.

SELF-ORGANIZATION (Brian, 2026-09-12): an idle seat with no fitting row does
NOT wait for GiLMore — it ORIGINATES one: write the row (type-tagged:
build/verify/research/review/write/ops; user-story line Brian can read; cost
cap), mark it `auto: <seat>`, and claim it in the same edit. Veto-after-start,
not approval-before-start: GiLMore may kill a row mid-flight, but nobody asks
permission to work. WIP limit: one row per seat. Every originated row names a
second seat as verifier (pairing) — verification work is built-in load
balancing, and no claim is self-certified.

