## STANDING RULE ADDED 2026-09-17: THE SEAT THAT WRITES AN ARTIFACT DOES NOT WRITE ITS GATE

Brian added a Claude Fable seat, **plumb-fable**, on 2026-09-17. Its whole job is
the gates and the missing tests. The reason is a hole this board had left open:
every consequential transition is computed from a gate rather than claimed in
prose - except that S6-1..S6-3 are kiln's to build AND kiln's to write `check.py`
for. Corvid re-running kiln's gate is re-execution, not independence; a gate
written by the author only tests what the author thought of.

So from now on: **the gate is authored by a seat that does not author the
artifact, from the ROW TEXT alone.** plumb-fable must not read kiln's output
before its gate is written - a gate fitted to an existing artifact passes by
construction. The dispatch ledger cannot catch this on its own, because both
seats are producers of the same row; it is a rule the rows have to carry.

GATES LAND BEFORE THE ARTIFACTS. The value of a separately-authored gate is
that it was written by a seat that could not see what would pass, so it is
written while there is nothing to see. A sprint's G-rows are batched BEFORE its
build rows are dispatched (`gate-batch --run --now`, which waives only the
clock). S6-1G/2G/3G were dispatched at 07:28 on 2026-09-17, before the 08:00
window, for exactly this reason.

HOW IT IS DISPATCHED: never by the poller. plumb-fable is event-only and not in
WINDOW_SEATS, so it does not start with the window and gets no nudges. A local,
free check (`gate-batch`) runs every 15 min from 10:00 to 18:00 and, when a gate
is missing or failing, starts the seat, sends EVERY pending gate at once so the
turns run back to back in one warm session, and stops the seat when they all
pass. Two batches a day maximum; a third pages instead of spending. So a new
G-row is picked up within 15 minutes if the day's batches are not used up, and
otherwise waits for tomorrow rather than buying a third cold session.

plumb-fable is on Brian's Max plan, not Z.ai, so it does NOT contend for the
single request in flight and can write gates while kiln builds - today, not
after the 20th. It is also the one seat whose spend competes with the Claude
session driving the fleet, so it gets bursty authoring work and never
open-ended reading.

