## SPRINT 5 GOAL — small on purpose (Brian, 2026-09-16)

**Re-run the cross-engine comparison on reader paths that iteration 1 already
validated, and decide what to publish.** Two rows: S4-14 (the re-run) and S4-15
(the base policy file). Nothing else is admitted to this sprint.

Why it is this small: Sprint 4's headline was "two memory systems scored 0/30
while a keyword baseline scored 25/30". That zero is very likely a known
configuration artifact. `team/ECOSYSTEM-MAP.md`, written 2026-09-13 — three days
before S4-12 ran — records `pi_lcm_store_reader` raw at **0.0** against
`pi_lcm_store_reader_toollevel` at **0.2227**, and records claude-mem at hit@5
**0.208** with its default 90-day window versus **0.958** with the window off,
plus a note that claude-mem "refuses raw — no supported no-LLM raw path".

S4-12 cited none of it. The knowledge was not missing; it was written down, in
the right file, by the right people, three days early — and nobody opened it
before re-measuring. That is the failure of this sprint, and it is the same
failure the whole bake-off exists to study.

**So the standing rule from here: a row that re-measures anything must cite the
prior measurement, or state in writing that none exists.**

**Second standing rule, 2026-09-16: a declared check must not depend on who runs
it.** No `$HOME`, no relative-to-cwd assumptions - absolute paths only. A worker
lane has its HOME redirected to its own sandbox, so `$HOME/.config/...` resolves
to a different place for a worker than for the poller, and the SAME declared
check then passes for one and fails for the other. S4-8's self-test check had
exactly this shape and corvid hit it as a permission error. A gate whose answer
depends on the caller is not a gate. A re-run that does
not say what it expects to differ from is not a measurement, it is a guess with
a number attached.

The sprint is done when the re-run reports old and new numbers side by side and
Brian has made the publish call. If a system still scores zero after using the
validated path, the row must demonstrate it returning something non-empty
through the harness before that zero is reported as a finding.

